{
  "description": "Mobile 390x844 portrait, DPR 3, touch, R-30: multi-point lines by taps and the line editor by touch. Taps the Arrow tool and saves its ARIA and a capture, then taps (60,200) with it; picks the Line tool by name and taps (60,280), (200,320) and (320,280); then draws a line by a drag from (60,420) to (300,420), double-taps its middle (two taps 120 ms apart) to open the line editor, and drags from the middle to (180,360), which adds a point if the editor shows a midpoint handle there and otherwise moves the line. Reads the scene, with each line's point count, and the app state after each step. s22 found that a tap with the Arrow tool makes a 100 px arrow and that the Rectangle tool opens a Rectangle, Diamond and Ellipse choice, so the Line tool is looked for in the Arrow tool's choice. Runs right after 09 in a fresh session (zoom 1, scroll 0,0, empty canvas).",
